From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Philip Taron <philip.taron@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 17:17:13 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] detect PIV touches reported by libccid over Varlink

While a YubiKey waits for a touch on a smartcard command, such as a PIV
decryption by age-plugin-yubikey, it answers pcscd with CCID time
extensions about every 290 ms. Only pcscd sees them, because it holds
the USB device, so none of the existing detectors can.

A libccid built with its varlink option reports them on the Varlink
socket /run/pcscd/ccid-touch, interface io.github.philiptaron.CcidTouch.
Follow its Watch stream and emit PIV_1/PIV_0 (reason "piv", D-Bus
property PIVState) while any Yubico reader is waiting.

pcscd exits when idle and the socket comes back when it restarts, so
reconnect when the socket is created (inotify on its directory), with a
30 s retry as a fallback. Without the socket, the detector stays idle.
