 This detection is based on the observation that a certain `/dev/hidraw*` device will disappear when YubiKey will start waiting for a HMAC, and reappear when it stops waiting for a touch.
 
+### Detecting PIV operations
+
+While a YubiKey waits for a touch on a smartcard command, such as a PIV decryption by `age-plugin-yubikey`, it answers `pcscd` with CCID time extensions, about every 290 ms. Only `pcscd` can see them, because it holds the USB device, so this detector needs a `libccid` built with its `varlink` option, which reports them on the Varlink socket `/run/pcscd/ccid-touch` (override with `$YUBIKEY_TOUCH_DETECTOR_CCID_SOCKET`). Readers from vendors other than Yubico are ignored. Without that socket, this detector stays idle.
+
